  "Number": 20,
  "Question": "If \\(4^x-4^{x-1}=24,\\) then \\((2x)^x\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\sqrt5\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\sqrt5\\)",
    "C": "\\(25\\sqrt5\\)",
    "D": "\\(125\\)",
    "E": "\\(25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The exponents differ by one, so \\(4^x=4\\cdot4^{x-1}\\). This lets us factor the subtraction:\n\\[\n4^x-4^{x-1}\n=(4-1)4^{x-1}=24.\n\\]\nThus \\(4^{x-1}=8\\). Writing both sides as powers of \\(2\\) gives\n\\[\n2^{2x-2}=2^3.\n\\]\nPowers of \\(2\\) increase strictly with their exponents, so their equality implies\n\\[\n2x-2=3,\n\\qquad x=\\frac52.\n\\]\nNow \\(2x=5>0\\), and the fractional exponent gives\n\\[\n(2x)^x=5^{5/2}=5^2\\sqrt{5}=25\\sqrt{5}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice C.",
